{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1188","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Count Pairs"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"prime"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number $$$p$$$, $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$, and an integer $$$k$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the number of pairs of indexes $$$(i, j)$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\lt j \\le n$$$) for which $$$(a_i + a_j)(a_i^2 + a_j^2) \\equiv k \\bmod p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integers $$$n, p, k$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$2 \\le p \\le 10^9$$$, $$$0 \\le k \\le p-1$$$). $$$p$$$ is guaranteed to be prime."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le p-1$$$). It is guaranteed that all elements are different."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3 0\n0 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 7 2\n1 2 3 4 5 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0+1)(0^2 + 1^2) = 1 \\equiv 1 \\bmod 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0+2)(0^2 + 2^2) = 8 \\equiv 2 \\bmod 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(1+2)(1^2 + 2^2) = 15 \\equiv 0 \\bmod 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So only $$$1$$$ pair satisfies the condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$3$$$ such pairs: $$$(1, 5)$$$, $$$(2, 3)$$$, $$$(4, 6)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1188B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1188/problem/B"}